IT DEPARTMENT – SAMPLE POLICY DOCUMENT

1. Purpose
This document defines basic IT policies to ensure system security, availability, and data integrity across the organization.

2. Server Patch Management
All production servers must be patched with the latest security updates at least once every month.
Critical security patches must be applied within 48 hours of release.
Failure to apply patches may expose systems to vulnerabilities, malware, or unauthorized access.

3. Data Backup and Recovery
Daily automated backups must be performed for all critical systems and databases.
Backups must be stored securely and tested quarterly to ensure successful recovery.
Lack of proper backups may result in data loss and business disruption.

4. Access Control
User access to systems must follow the principle of least privilege.
Administrative access should be reviewed every quarter.
Unauthorized or excessive access can lead to data breaches or compliance violations.

5. Incident Management
All security incidents must be reported to the IT team within 24 hours.
Incidents should be logged, investigated, and resolved with corrective actions documented.

End of Document
